questions.q:
A page runs this code:

goto = location.hash.slice(1)
if (goto.startsWith('https:')) {
  location = goto;
}

Which link would redirect a victim to https://www.evil-user.net?

Why is this listener vulnerable?

window.addEventListener('message', function(e) {
  eval(e.data);
});

Identify the source and the sink in this vulnerable code:

let url = /https?:\/\/.+/.exec(location.hash);
if (url) {
  location = url[0];
}

A page contains:

window.onload = function(){
  let someObject = window.someObject || {};
  let script = document.createElement('script');
  script.src = someObject.url;
  document.body.appendChild(script);
};

The HTML filter blocks scripts but allows id and name attributes. Which injected HTML makes the page load //malicious-website.com/evil.js?
